==================================================================
DAY 54 - PART B: LAB
Deploy from Git with Argo CD
Time: 90-120 minutes
==================================================================

STEP 0: Push your repo to GitHub
--------------------------------
Create a PUBLIC repo on GitHub named k8s-journey (public keeps the lab
simple; private repos need credentials in Argo CD).
Make sure no secrets/keys are committed (check .gitignore, git log).
  cd ~/k8s-journey
  git remote add origin https://github.com/<you>/k8s-journey.git
  git branch -M main
  git push -u origin main


STEP 1: Install Argo CD
-----------------------
k create ns argocd
k apply -n argocd -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml
k get pods -n argocd -w

CLI:
  curl -sSL -o argocd https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/releases/latest/download/argocd-linux-amd64
  sudo install -m 555 argocd /usr/local/bin/argocd ; rm argocd

UI:
  k port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443 &
  PASS=$(k -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath='{.data.password}' | base64 -d); echo $PASS
  Open https://localhost:8080 (accept the self-signed cert), user admin.
  argocd login localhost:8080 --username admin --password $PASS --insecure


STEP 2: Your first Application
------------------------------
mkdir -p ~/k8s-journey/week8/argocd && cd $_
vi app-dev.yaml

apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: myapp-dev
  namespace: argocd
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/<you>/k8s-journey.git
    targetRevision: main
    path: week8/kustomize/overlays/dev
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: kz-dev
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true
      selfHeal: true
    syncOptions:
    - CreateNamespace=true

k apply -f app-dev.yaml
argocd app list
argocd app get myapp-dev
k get all -n kz-dev
In the UI: the tree of Deployment -> ReplicaSet -> Pods.


STEP 3: Change Git, watch the cluster follow
--------------------------------------------
Edit week8/kustomize/overlays/dev/kustomization.yaml: add
  replicas:
  - name: myapp
    count: 3
git commit -am "dev: 3 replicas" && git push
Argo CD polls every ~3 minutes (or click Refresh / argocd app sync myapp-dev):
  k get pods -n kz-dev -w


STEP 4: Self-heal (drift)
-------------------------
k scale deploy myapp -n kz-dev --replicas=1
k get pods -n kz-dev -w        # back to 3 within seconds
k delete svc myapp -n kz-dev
k get svc -n kz-dev            # recreated
The cluster obeys Git, not kubectl.


STEP 5: Prune
-------------
Remove service.yaml from base/kustomization.yaml resources, commit,
push, sync: the Service is deleted from the cluster. Revert it:
  git revert HEAD && git push


STEP 6: Rollback = git revert
-----------------------------
Change GREETING in the dev overlay, push, check the app. Then:
  git log --oneline -3
  git revert <commit> && git push
argocd app history myapp-dev


STEP 7: A Helm-based Application (your chart from Day 51)
---------------------------------------------------------
vi app-helm.yaml

apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: myapp-helm
  namespace: argocd
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/<you>/k8s-journey.git
    targetRevision: main
    path: week8/charts/myapp
    helm:
      valueFiles:
      - values.yaml
      parameters:
      - name: greeting
        value: "Deployed by Argo CD from a Helm chart"
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: helm-argo
  syncPolicy:
    automated: {prune: true, selfHeal: true}
    syncOptions: [CreateNamespace=true]

k apply -f app-helm.yaml ; argocd app get myapp-helm


STEP 8: Manage the Applications from Git too (app of apps)
----------------------------------------------------------
Commit app-dev.yaml and app-helm.yaml into week8/argocd/apps/ and
create ONE root Application pointing at that folder. From now on,
adding an Application = adding a file in Git.


STEP 9: Clean up and commit
---------------------------
argocd app delete myapp-helm --yes
(keep myapp-dev for tomorrow)
cd ~/k8s-journey && git add . && git commit -m "day54: argocd" && git push
